A file that declares :PUBLIC MYUSERNAME is the initializer that creates
the global, so its assignment is not diag.global_assignment (issue #169);
each :PUBLIC statement still fires diag.limit_public_vars (info tier) on its keyword,
one per statement however many names it lists.
-- input.ssl --
:PUBLIC MYUSERNAME;
:PUBLIC gSiteCode, gShiftNo;
MYUSERNAME := "system";
gSiteCode := "S01";
gShiftNo := 1;
-- format --
:PUBLIC MYUSERNAME;
:PUBLIC gSiteCode, gShiftNo;

MYUSERNAME := "system";
gSiteCode := "S01";
gShiftNo := 1;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:8 info limit_public_vars: ':PUBLIC' variables persist across procedures and risk namespace pollution. Prefer ':DECLARE' with parameter passing
2:1-2:8 info limit_public_vars: ':PUBLIC' variables persist across procedures and risk namespace pollution. Prefer ':DECLARE' with parameter passing
